meta {
  name: 06 Brief on chart open
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

get {
  url: {{openemr_base}}{{module_path}}/api/session.php
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  The panel does not decide for itself that a pre-visit brief should be
  prepared: `BriefPolicy` decides server-side, under the physician's own
  session, and `brief_on_open` is the answer the panel obeys (ADR-0003
  amendment, module 0.5.0).

  Run this after `02 Open Chart`. With the default
  `COPILOT_BRIEF_ON_OPEN=visit_today`, the flag is true only for a chart
  whose patient has a visit today, so on the seeded cohort it is normally
  false — that is the correct, cheap answer, not a failure. The assertions
  below check the contract (the field exists and is a boolean tied to an
  open chart), never a particular day's schedule.

  To see the true branch without waiting for a scheduled visit, an operator
  can set `COPILOT_BRIEF_ON_OPEN=always` on the openemr service; a front
  desk role gets `false` in every mode, because a brief it is not allowed
  to read would cost a denied turn and an audit row on every chart open.
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.chart_open: eq true
  res.body.brief_on_open: isBoolean
  res.body.module_version: isString
}
